# ★★★ dx-i2 — THE VITRINE'S LOOPBACK DOOR (service `storefront-loopback` in compose.yml).
#
# This caddy shares the VITRINE's network namespace and listens on the port of `FORGE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN`, so that
# `http://localhost:<port>` — the address the vitrine's warmer fetches every page at (`POST /api/warm` runs the
# fetches INSIDE the vitrine's container) — reaches this box's edge instead of the container itself. The why,
# the measurement (`planned=838 warmed=0`, every url ECONNREFUSED, 2026-10-10) and the derivation are in
# `env-source.sh`, at `_forge_loopback_door_port`.
#
# ⚠️ IT ADDS NOTHING TO THE EDGE. No port is published, no route is decided here: every request goes to the
# bench edge's shop face (`caddy:80`, `caddy/Caddyfile.local`), and `reverse_proxy` passes the Host header
# through unchanged by default, so the edge sees exactly the request a browser on this machine sends.
{
	auto_https off
	admin off
}

:{$FORGE_LOOPBACK_DOOR_PORT} {
	reverse_proxy caddy:80
}
